s the comparison fair? Are baselines appropriate?\n\n3. **Statistical rigor**: Given the small sample sizes (n=35-43 per model), are the conclusions adequately supported? Is the bootstrap analysis sufficient? How concerning are the wide CIs?\n\n4. **Reproducibility**: Is there enough detail to reproduce? Dataset availability? Hyperparameter reporting?\n\n5. **Presentation of results**: Are the 13 tables effectively organized? Too many? Information density?\n\n6. **Weaknesses**: List concrete, specific weaknesses with page/table references.\n\n7. **Questions for authors**: 3-5 specific questions.\n\n8. **Score**: Provide your score (1-6) with justification.\n\n9. **Confidence**: Rate your confidence (1-5: 1=low, 5=expert).\n\nFormat your review as a structured report with clear sections."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0185jgVWGRn68kcVV3gpuExJ","session_id":"d469ef9f-e126-42f2-b0c6-3a31ae100457","uuid":"c035efc6-9fce-4ee9-8fb5-d8bf2103e89a","timestamp":"2026-05-16T21:59:31.157Z"}
