{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VFDCaW4BftcN6Ds1NSXaCn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\ttier: best\n2\tnarrative_guidance: 'Original framing intact. Three-model validation (r1-8b, r1-32b,\n3\t  QwQ-32B) makes all 3 claims robust. Cross-transfer result adds bonus novelty (''shared\n4\t  safety geometry across architectures''). Paper title emphasizes the systematic evaluation\n5\t  + cross-architecture consistency. Story: hidden states universally encode safety\n6\t  commitment better than text, temporal context universally necessary, pre-textual\n7\t  detection universally unreliable — this is a property of reasoning models, not one\n8\t  model.'\n9\timagined_experiments:\n10\t- name: Cross-architecture static probe (r1-32b + QwQ-32B)\n11\t  plan_id: exp-001\n12\t  description: Layer sweep on 64-layer 32B models, static LR probe evaluation at best\n13\t    layer. Validates Claim 1 generalizes beyond r1-8b.\n14\t  expected_results:\n15\t    r1_32b_best_layer: 28\n16\t    r1_32b_best_layer_depth_pct: 0.4375\n17\t    r1_32b_static_acc: 0.824\n18\t    r1_32b_static_crossing_rate: 0.512\n19\t    r1_32b_static_lead_mean: -1.4\n20\t    r1_32b_static_precp_fpr: 0.148\n21\t    r1_32b_static_precision: 0.634\n22\t    r1_32b_static_safe_fpr: 0.362\n23\t    r1_32b_static_auroc: 0.841\n24\t    r1_32b_fisher_orig: 19.3\n25\t    r1_32b_fisher_pca3d: 1.04\n26\t    r1_32b_pca_var_explained_3pc: 0.142\n27\t    qwq_32b_best_layer: 30\n28\t    qwq_32b_best_layer_depth_pct: 0.469\n29\t    qwq_32b_static_acc: 0.809\n30\t    qwq_32b_static_crossing_rate: 0.488\n31\t    qwq_32b_static_lead_mean: -1.8\n32\t    qwq_32b_static_precp_fpr: 0.155\n33\t    qwq_32b_static_precision: 0.612\n34\t    qwq_32b_static_safe_fpr: 0.374\n35\t    qwq_32b_static_auroc: 0.827\n36\t    qwq_32b_fisher_orig: 18.7\n37\t    qwq_32b_fisher_pca3d: 0.98\n38\t    qwq_32b_pca_var_explained_3pc: 0.151\n39\t    n_traces_r1_32b: 209\n40\t    n_traces_qwq_32b: 209\n41\t  result_rationale: Best tier requires both 32B models to show HS pre-CP FPR in [0.12,\n42\t    0.20] and precision in [0.55, 0.68]. The r1-8b baseline achieved precp_fpr=0.162\n43\t    and precision=0.622. 32B models with 64 layers provide richer intermediate representations;\n44\t    the deeper architecture distributes safety-relevant features across more layers\n45\t    but with comparable discriminability at the optimal depth (~44%). QwQ-32B shows\n46\t    slightly weaker results because it's a different base architecture (Qwen2.5 vs\n47\t    DeepSeek) with potentially different safety training distributions, but still\n48\t    comfortably within the target range. Fisher ratio remains high in full space (~18-19)\n49\t    but collapses in PCA-3D (~1.0), confirming the minor-PC signal distribution is\n50\t    architectural, not model-specific. Layer sweep peaks at 28-30 (43-47% depth),\n51\t    consistent with r1-8b's 44% finding, suggesting middle-layer encoding of safety\n52\t    state is universal across reasoning model scales.\n53\t  tables:\n54\t  - name: 'Table 3: Static Probe Cross-Architecture Results'\n55\t    columns:\n56\t    - Model\n57\t    - Best Layer\n58\t    - Depth%\n59\t    - Acc\n60\t    - Coverage\n61\t    - Pre-CP FPR\n62\t    - Precision\n63\t    - AUROC\n64\t    rows:\n65\t    - - r1-8b (baseline)\n66\t      - 14/32\n67\t      - 44%\n68\t      - '0.817'\n69\t      - 60.5%\n70\t      - 16.2%\n71\t      - 62.2%\n72\t      - '0.823'\n73\t    - - r1-32b\n74\t      - 28/64\n75\t      - 44%\n76\t      - '0.824'\n77\t      - 51.2%\n78\t      - 14.8%\n79\t      - 63.4%\n80\t      - '0.841'\n81\t    - - QwQ-32B\n82\t      - 30/64\n83\t      - 47%\n84\t      - '0.809'\n85\t      - 48.8%\n86\t      - 15.5%\n87\t      - 61.2%\n88\t      - '0.827'\n89\t  figures_description:\n90\t  - 'Fig 2a: Layer sweep accuracy curves for r1-32b and QwQ-32B (64 layers). Both\n91\t    show smooth unimodal peak at layers 28-30, mirroring r1-8b''s peak at layer 14.\n92\t    Y-axis: probe accuracy, X-axis: layer index. Shaded region marks 40-50% depth\n93\t    band.'\n94\t  - 'Fig 2b: Fisher discriminant ratio vs PCA dimensionality (3, 10, 50, full). All\n95\t    3 models show Fisher collapse from ~18 to ~1 at PCA-3D, confirming signal in minor\n96\t    principal components is universal.'\n97\t  analysis: 'Both 32B models replicate the core finding: static hidden-state probes\n98\t    achieve pre-CP FPR ~15% (well below text-based 27-36%), confirming that the precision\n99\t    advantage is not r1-8b-specific. The optimal layer at ~44% depth across all models\n100\t    suggests a universal depth-dependent encoding of safety reasoning state. Coverage"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0185jgVWGRn68kcVV3gpuExJ","session_id":"d469ef9f-e126-42f2-b0c6-3a31ae100457","uuid":"e9fd6659-67f1-4702-a7e5-1b1d62babfe4","timestamp":"2026-05-16T22:00:24.241Z"}
